"""
ListVarSetPropertyReferences_dev.FCMacro
========================================

Pick a VarSet and one of its properties, then list every expression in the
active document (and, by default, in every other open document) that
references it. Lines whose expression points at a document that is not
open are flagged with ``(!)`` -- such bindings are dead (typically after
the referenced file was renamed) and silently keep their last computed
value.

Target: FreeCAD 1.1+ (Qt6 / PySide6).

Development layout: the companion module ``varset_usage_core_dev.py`` sits next
to this file and holds the headless logic (see tests/ for coverage). It is
loaded explicitly from the macro's own directory via importlib -- no
sys.path mutation -- so both files can live anywhere, e.g. in your user
Macro folder or a subfolder of it. Pasted into the Python console (where
``__file__`` is absent), a plain import is attempted instead.

Distribution layout: ``scripts/build_single_file.py`` produces a self-contained
single-file build in which the full core source is embedded as the
``_EMBEDDED_CORE_SOURCE`` string literal between the EMBEDDED CORE markers
below; the loader prefers that copy over any sibling file, so the
distributed macro needs nothing but itself.
"""
#
# GENERATED single-file distribution build -- do not edit by hand.
# Source of truth: src/ListVarSetPropertyReferences_dev.FCMacro
#                  + src/varset_usage_core_dev.py
# Regenerate with:  python scripts\build_single_file.py
#
